    "text": "Let the circumcentre of a triangle with vertices <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>,</mo><mi>B</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>C</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mi>b</mi><mo>&#62;</mo><mn>0</mn></math>&nbsp;be <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi><mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>. If the line <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mi>P</mi></math>&nbsp;intersects the line <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi><mi>C</mi></math> at the point <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Q</mi><mfenced><mrow><msub><mi>k</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced></math>, then <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>k</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;is equal to",
